# ICDFA Lab 07 — Exploring ICS Packet Captures

## Overview

This lab focused on analyzing an instructor-provided Industrial Control
Systems (ICS) packet capture using **Wireshark**.

The objective was to identify different ICS and network protocols, inspect
their communication, and identify security-relevant information visible in
the captured traffic.

## Objectives

- Analyze ICS packet captures using Wireshark display filters.
- Identify HTTP, FTP, Modbus, DNP3, EtherNet/IP, and S7 communication.
- Identify exposed credentials, device metadata, and industrial operations.
- Understand security weaknesses associated with legacy and cleartext
  industrial protocols.
- Perform passive packet analysis without interacting with external systems.

## Environment

| Component | Details |
|---|---|
| Operating System | Kali Linux |
| Tool | Wireshark 4.6.6 |
| Capture | `ICDFA_Lab7ICS_Traffic.pcap` |
| Analysis Type | Passive Packet Analysis |

